Also read comments.html:13, where the byline holds the avatar, login, badge and time, and headless.go:98 (`--window-size=1024,1400`). Lesson #940 sets the window floor at 492 px. SL-007's validate-slice-1.json:60 shows that its harness drives Chrome over `--remote-debugging-port=0`.

verdicts.instead:
Make the Go test strict: fail if it finds any horizontal margin, padding or border on `.replies`, `.comment` or `main` other than the declarations it reads, shorthands included. Specify the validate look in full:
- set the 360 px and 400 px viewports with CDP `Emulation.setDeviceMetricsOverride` (mobile:true), not `--window-size`;
- seed a depth-5 branch page with a 39-character login, a long unbroken body, the Author badge and an open `details.reply`;
- assert `document.documentElement.scrollWidth <= innerWidth`, and the same at 1000 px.
If that fails on the login, the fix is `overflow-wrap: anywhere` (or min-width: 0) on `.login`, decided in the build, not found after it.

verdicts.why:
The oracle follows Location, GETs it, and asserts that `comment-<id>` is drawn with its body. It never checks the fragment, which is the part that puts the reader on the comment. These would all pass:
- a redirect to the right branch page with `#comment-<ancestor>`;
- a handler that always takes the `#comments` fallback, for every D ≤ cap, because /reports/x draws those depths;
- a target LocalPath refuses: it becomes '/', and when x is the newest report, '/' draws D ≤ cap.

'Not inside a cut node' is true by construction, because a cut node renders no child articles. It adds no strength.

verdicts.instead:
For each D, parse Location. Assert:
- the fragment is exactly `comment-<id>`;
- the path is /reports/x when D ≤ threadDepthCap, otherwise /reports/x/comments/<n>, where n is an id in the chain;
- the GET of that path answers 200 and draws `comment-<id>` as a non-placeholder article whose own text holds the body.
Keep the nil-path row (blocked poster → `/reports/x#comment-<id>`) with the same exact-Location assertion.

